WEBVTT

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:05.670
Infinite Ryvius

00:00:05.670 --> 00:00:09.030
What do they mean "the guys
on Ryvius are terrorists"?

00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:12.330
The news must be mistaken.
We've done nothing.

00:00:12.470 --> 00:00:15.240
But it's a fact that we
beat up the Mars Forces.

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:17.780
We shouldn't have used the Vital Guarder.

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:20.610
But they're the ones that attacked us.
What other choice did we have?

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:22.940
So we've all become criminals, have we?

00:00:23.150 --> 00:00:24.740
They're just making a big mistake!

00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:27.850
But what if there really
are terrorists aboard?

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:30.420
It could be the Zwei, you know.

00:00:30.490 --> 00:00:32.360
Then the supervisors are also suspicious.

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:35.300
It's no use! All the routes to
the bridge have been closed off!

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:38.750
Those damn Zwei! They tricked us
all along knowing we knew nothing!

00:00:38.830 --> 00:00:41.800
I wanna go home! I wanna go home!

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:43.400
Shut up! Stop crying!

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:45.210
I'm telling you, don't cry!

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:46.500
We're doomed!

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:54.280
<i>Think. Think this through.</i>
<i>About what we can do right now.</i>

00:00:55.180 --> 00:00:55.740
<i>But!</i>

00:00:56.680 --> 00:00:59.850
<i>What is there that we can do?</i>
<i>That I can do... now...?</i>

00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:04.550
Infinite Ryvius

00:01:05.260 --> 00:01:12.130
If you're going to walk, right here will be fine

00:01:13.130 --> 00:01:16.140
Although loneliness...

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:20.470
...can sometimes be unbearable

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:27.710
There's the benefit of not hurting anyone...

00:01:28.850 --> 00:01:32.790
...and the benefit of not being exposed...

00:01:32.790 --> 00:01:35.760
...and hurt by others as well

00:01:36.260 --> 00:01:43.290
At the opposite side of the frozen sea...

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:47.070
...the dream and the reality...

00:01:47.070 --> 00:01:50.700
...that you saw cross paths

00:01:50.870 --> 00:01:54.400
Some light is shed...

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:58.980
...but how it is done is unknown...

00:01:58.980 --> 00:02:06.220
...so that we can go to a different place

00:02:06.690 --> 00:02:14.220
The things I want have no shape

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:22.630
Tear the final universe, today until tomorrow

00:02:33.210 --> 00:02:36.650
Whereabouts of the Future

00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:43.850
Ryvius's actions are nothing more than
direct violence pointed at the Alliance...

00:02:44.090 --> 00:02:47.120
...resulting from a willful misinterpretation
of the Alliance's ideals.

00:02:47.530 --> 00:02:51.520
We must take a firm stance
against such aggressive actions!

00:02:51.970 --> 00:02:56.270
The Alliance is calling out
to all planets and satellites...

00:02:56.540 --> 00:02:58.870
...for their full cooperation
in capturing the Ryvius...!

00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:00.270
They're in complete
control of the situation.

00:03:00.470 --> 00:03:04.810
Honestly, I didn't expect them
to be this well prepared.

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:06.650
We're being forestalled in every attempt.

00:03:06.650 --> 00:03:09.050
However, paradoxically speaking...

00:03:09.380 --> 00:03:12.480
...this would mean the Ryvius is still
out there sailing on its own.

00:03:12.790 --> 00:03:14.340
So the opportunity still exists.

00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:16.560
Did you get the documents?

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:20.960
Yes. We were able to obtain a copy of the
Orbital Security Bureau's operation report.

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:24.770
See to it that the bereaved
family is well compensated.

00:03:24.770 --> 00:03:25.960
It's being looked after, sir.

00:03:29.270 --> 00:03:30.760
<i>Mission Code: Vecker.</i>

00:03:31.410 --> 00:03:33.500
<i>Plan drafted Earth Standard</i>
<i>Time October 21, 2223.</i>

00:03:33.710 --> 00:03:40.010
<i>Six months later, initial phase commences.</i>

00:03:40.810 --> 00:03:43.820
<i>Two special agents of the Orbital</i>
<i>Security Bureau sneak into...</i>

00:03:43.820 --> 00:03:46.380
<i>... the Astronaut Training Center,</i>
<i>Liebe Delta as staff members.</i>

00:03:46.820 --> 00:03:49.390
<i>The purpose, to change</i>
<i>Liebe Delta's course...</i>

00:03:49.390 --> 00:03:51.820
<i>... and capture a Vaia ship concealed within.</i>

00:03:52.860 --> 00:03:55.660
<i>April 28, 2225, in accordance with plans...</i>

00:03:56.060 --> 00:04:01.500
<i>... Liebe Delta descended into Sere One to</i>
<i>restore energy and drop the center pillar...</i>

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:04.790
<i>... worn down as a result of exposure to</i>
<i>the Geduld. The "Dive" takes place.</i>

00:04:05.610 --> 00:04:10.010
<i>Most of the staff and students were</i>
<i>on a break and had returned home.</i>

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:12.550
<i>According to the shuttles'</i>
<i>passenger lists...</i>

00:04:12.550 --> 00:04:16.850
<i>... it is assumed there were 68 staff</i>
<i>members and 534 students remaining...</i>

00:04:17.020 --> 00:04:19.990
<i>... for a total of 602 people on board.</i>

00:04:21.390 --> 00:04:24.190
You abandoned the lives of over
600 people for a mere operation?

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:26.750
Berkovich, you bastard.

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:32.100
<i>15:48 on that day,</i>
<i>second phase commences.</i>

00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:36.090
<i>In order to make it appear that Liebe Delta</i>
<i>was crushed in a "Dive" accident...</i>

00:04:36.470 --> 00:04:39.440
<i>... the agents succeed in changing the</i>
<i>depth to which Liebe Delta would sink.</i>

00:04:40.110 --> 00:04:43.710
<i>At the same time, submersible ship</i>
<i>Tandel, of the Orbital Security Bureau...</i>

00:04:43.710 --> 00:04:45.680
<i>... commences its part of the operation.</i>

00:04:46.310 --> 00:04:49.420
<i>Tandel had been in the area on</i>
<i>its own for the last two weeks...</i>

00:04:49.420 --> 00:04:52.010
<i>... their official mission to</i>
<i>take part in a mock battle.</i>

00:04:52.550 --> 00:04:55.020
<i>The Captain, Commander</i>
<i>Conrad Viscuess.</i>

00:04:58.330 --> 00:05:00.920
<i>On the 29th of that month, at 5:21,</i>
<i>on the brink of being crushed...</i>

00:05:01.330 --> 00:05:07.670
<i>... the crew of Liebe Delta dares a purge</i>
<i>in order to reduce its speed of descent.</i>

00:05:08.340 --> 00:05:12.070
<i>At 5:28, all but a portion of Liebe Delta's</i>
<i>central pillar continues its descent...</i>

00:05:12.410 --> 00:05:14.700
<i>... at a speed of 0.001 herschels...</i>

00:05:15.180 --> 00:05:18.200
<i>... from the point Sere Two, 367.</i>

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:22.310
<i>On April 30, at 3:23...</i>

00:05:22.980 --> 00:05:27.220
<i>... on the verge of entering Sere 3, Tandel</i>
<i>succeeds in connecting with Liebe Delta.</i>

00:05:28.090 --> 00:05:31.110
<i>Tandel proceeds with its plan to crush the</i>
<i>central pillar concealing the Vaia ship.</i>

00:05:32.890 --> 00:05:35.330
<i>At 3:35, they disconnect.</i>

00:05:36.330 --> 00:05:40.460
<i>The reason: The Vaia ship hidden within</i>
<i>the central pillar had been activated.</i>

00:05:41.300 --> 00:05:44.790
<i>At this time, Tandel confirms an increase</i>
<i>in neutrino and gravitational waves.</i>

00:05:46.410 --> 00:05:48.140
<i>The Vaia ship begins its ascent...</i>

00:05:48.580 --> 00:05:53.040
<i>... and at 9:44, escapes</i>
<i>Geduld into ordinary space.</i>

00:05:55.180 --> 00:05:59.020
<i>4 days after Liebe Delta's</i>
<i>destruction, on 13:18 of May 2...</i>

00:05:59.750 --> 00:06:01.980
<i>... Mission Plan YS-45 commences.</i>

00:06:03.120 --> 00:06:07.080
<i>Two preceding scouting boats succeed</i>
<i>in a rendezvous with the Vaia ship...</i>

00:06:07.790 --> 00:06:09.460
<i>... and succeed in electro-magnetically</i>
<i>capturing the ship.</i>

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:12.490
<i>On 13:56 of the same day...</i>

00:06:13.270 --> 00:06:15.890
<i>... the Vaia ship develops a gravitational</i>
<i>field with a radius of 70 kilometers.</i>

00:06:16.370 --> 00:06:18.440
<i>The approaching two scouting boats...</i>

00:06:18.440 --> 00:06:20.130
<i>... were sucked into the field.</i>

00:06:20.440 --> 00:06:24.770
<i>Abend 1 and Abend 2 were destroyed.</i>

00:06:26.210 --> 00:06:28.340
<i>Mission failure.</i>

00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:29.950
<i>Twelve minutes later...</i>

00:06:29.950 --> 00:06:32.480
<i>... the Vaia ship submerges</i>
<i>itself into the Geduld...</i>

00:06:33.750 --> 00:06:35.780
<i>... and disappears out of sight.</i>

00:06:42.530 --> 00:06:46.730
<i>The system that had functioned just once,</i>
<i>twelve years ago, is now fully operational.</i>

00:06:47.470 --> 00:06:50.440
<i>However, there needs to be</i>
<i>a Sphix for it to operate.</i>

00:06:51.440 --> 00:06:53.270
<i>Who in the world is controlling the system?</i>

00:06:54.980 --> 00:06:57.000
<i>Who's controlling the Ryvius?</i>

00:06:59.880 --> 00:07:02.220
Things like the enemy's vessel
model being displayed as unknown...

00:07:02.220 --> 00:07:05.840
...or the data on our shield being changed,
were all steps intended to deceive us.

00:07:06.590 --> 00:07:09.250
That would explain why
we're receiving no response...

00:07:09.860 --> 00:07:11.820
...even though we continuously
sent out rescue signals.

00:07:12.260 --> 00:07:17.360
They probably took over all
communication relay iridium systems...

00:07:17.900 --> 00:07:20.590
...within the Solar System and
intercepted only our messages.

00:07:21.200 --> 00:07:25.400
That means our enemy is powerful enough
to control the Orbital Security Bureau.

00:07:25.870 --> 00:07:26.710
Damn you!

00:07:26.710 --> 00:07:30.540
Does knowledge of that fact change
our present situation in any way?

00:07:30.780 --> 00:07:31.900
You fool!

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:34.700
We've quickly changed from
refugees to terrorists.

00:07:34.950 --> 00:07:37.180
Well, we did do something
that would label us as such.

00:07:37.380 --> 00:07:39.380
Wait a minute! Are you
saying this is our fault?

00:07:39.690 --> 00:07:42.220
You're the ones who forcefully
ordered us to pilot the Vital Guarder!

00:07:42.220 --> 00:07:44.090
What good is it to argue about
what's already happened?

00:07:44.890 --> 00:07:47.880
Please. Let's concentrate on
what we'll do from this point on.

00:07:48.230 --> 00:07:53.030
That's right! Unless we do something,
we could be facing a riot aboard the ship!

00:07:53.300 --> 00:07:54.800
Who are you to talk?

00:07:54.800 --> 00:07:57.860
This is all the result of you pulling the
trigger to the main cannon, you know!

00:07:58.170 --> 00:07:59.410
Huh? But that...!

00:07:59.410 --> 00:08:01.200
You were very brave, Charlie.

00:08:01.840 --> 00:08:02.600
Stupid girl.

00:08:19.530 --> 00:08:23.550
In any case, it's a fact that we've been
declared as terrorists on the news.

00:08:25.100 --> 00:08:28.470
Right now, we are left
with only three options.

00:08:29.270 --> 00:08:32.760
First, we can force our way onto Mars,
and explain our side of the story.

00:08:33.470 --> 00:08:37.970
Second, leave the vicinity of Mars and
search for a planet that will accept us.

00:08:38.850 --> 00:08:41.680
And third, abandon this ship and surrender.

00:08:45.390 --> 00:08:48.720
I imagine the Ryvius would be too big
to attempt a forceful landing on Mars.

00:08:49.120 --> 00:08:52.060
You fool. This ship has
gravitational control capabilities.

00:08:52.630 --> 00:08:54.750
It would have no problem entering
an atmosphere like that of Mars.

00:08:55.330 --> 00:08:58.330
We could also submit the logbook
of the Ryvius in accordance with...

00:08:58.330 --> 00:09:00.230
...the Space Navigational Laws.

00:09:00.570 --> 00:09:02.430
And take it to Space Navigation Court?

00:09:03.100 --> 00:09:04.970
They don't even respond to our messages.

00:09:05.370 --> 00:09:07.400
I can't assume they'd be
willing to talk with us.

00:09:08.170 --> 00:09:10.610
I don't think the first
choice is an option either.

00:09:10.910 --> 00:09:13.540
Then do we leave here and go elsewhere?

00:09:14.080 --> 00:09:16.050
Will the people on board
from Mars approve it?

00:09:16.520 --> 00:09:20.510
Besides, if we ran away, it would be like
telling them that we are in fact terrorists.

00:09:20.890 --> 00:09:22.450
Then our only option is to surrender.

00:09:22.720 --> 00:09:26.160
Get out! <i>That</i> would be
telling them we're criminals.

00:09:26.390 --> 00:09:28.760
Yeah, I'd hate to think
how they'd treat us.

00:09:29.360 --> 00:09:31.630
I don't wanna sit here and die,
not able to do anything!

00:09:33.770 --> 00:09:36.070
Kouji. What's everyone's opinion like?

00:09:36.740 --> 00:09:40.300
I only have responses
from 237 people, of those...

00:09:40.470 --> 00:09:43.310
...80 percent want us to ask for protection
from Mars or the Orbital Security Bureau.

00:09:43.710 --> 00:09:44.980
Are they outta their minds?

00:09:44.980 --> 00:09:48.210
Don't they understand that we're
being looked upon as terrorists?!

00:09:48.880 --> 00:09:50.040
They don't understand the reality of it all.

00:09:50.750 --> 00:09:52.910
The majority weren't involved
in the actual battle.

00:09:53.450 --> 00:09:56.250
Airs Blue. What's your opinion on this?

00:09:56.860 --> 00:09:59.320
I have no opinion. You guys decide.

00:10:02.400 --> 00:10:06.060
Yuki. You've been awfully quiet.
Don't you have an opinion?

00:10:06.270 --> 00:10:07.300
Not really.

00:10:07.300 --> 00:10:09.600
It's a problem that means our lives, Yuki!

00:10:09.900 --> 00:10:11.170
What's the use?

00:10:11.170 --> 00:10:14.660
No matter what I say, it's gonna
be the way this guy wants it.

00:10:21.010 --> 00:10:22.450
Say something!

00:10:28.920 --> 00:10:30.510
That was a wonderful speech, sir.

00:10:30.890 --> 00:10:34.050
We're continuing our under the table
negotiations with the respective planets...

00:10:34.590 --> 00:10:37.960
...so we should be able to make an
official announcement in a few days.

00:10:40.170 --> 00:10:41.390
What's the latest from the Lab?

00:10:42.100 --> 00:10:45.470
All materials relating to the
operation have been delivered.

00:10:46.110 --> 00:10:49.100
You should be able to view specific
data by the day after tomorrow.

00:10:50.540 --> 00:10:53.440
I trust you've deleted all material
on correspondence from the Bratica.

00:10:53.850 --> 00:10:55.280
As planned, sir.

00:10:55.480 --> 00:10:59.280
We will capture the Bratica, no matter
what disgrace we must live with.

00:11:00.050 --> 00:11:02.560
There's no going back,
now that we've come this far.

00:11:02.560 --> 00:11:05.420
Even if the Geduld
Phenomenon was to reoccur.

00:11:06.190 --> 00:11:07.990
I understand, sir.

00:11:20.710 --> 00:11:24.010
This all happened because
I'm away from the bridge.

00:11:24.280 --> 00:11:25.040
What do you mean?

00:11:25.880 --> 00:11:29.140
It's nothing you need to know.
You don't have to know.

00:11:30.850 --> 00:11:32.650
Father... Mother...

00:11:37.690 --> 00:11:39.090
Infinite Ryvius

00:11:42.430 --> 00:11:43.830
Infinite Ryvius

00:11:54.770 --> 00:11:58.340
<i>Damn Yuki. When will you realize</i>
<i>that you can't beat Blue?</i>

00:11:59.050 --> 00:12:00.840
If we can't descend onto Mars...

00:12:01.780 --> 00:12:04.480
...and we don't wanna surrender,
we've only got one option left.

00:12:05.220 --> 00:12:06.890
We should escape from here.

00:12:06.890 --> 00:12:08.150
Escape to where?

00:12:08.150 --> 00:12:09.560
Anywhere will do.

00:12:09.560 --> 00:12:12.460
The important thing is to ensure
the safety of everyone aboard.

00:12:13.030 --> 00:12:14.860
Can we persuade the people on board?

00:12:15.230 --> 00:12:16.860
We'll make them understand.

00:12:17.200 --> 00:12:19.690
We'll say something like "the Mars Space
Navigation Forces are attacking us".

00:12:19.930 --> 00:12:21.330
Are you suggesting that we lie?

00:12:21.330 --> 00:12:22.820
But it's an effective method.

00:12:23.540 --> 00:12:26.730
We have control of all information
coming into this ship.

00:12:27.240 --> 00:12:28.980
We can say whatever we wish.

00:12:28.980 --> 00:12:31.940
We'd be better off looking for someone
that will help us after we escape.

00:12:33.250 --> 00:12:36.680
I like that option. If worse comes
to worse, we can abandon this ship.

00:12:37.050 --> 00:12:39.450
You're right. That works best.

00:12:39.650 --> 00:12:41.550
Odds for survival are greater.

00:12:41.820 --> 00:12:42.490
No objection.

00:12:42.490 --> 00:12:44.290
It'll have to do. Let's do it.

00:12:44.560 --> 00:12:45.660
I agree.

00:12:45.660 --> 00:12:47.160
Then we should make an announcement.

00:12:47.160 --> 00:12:48.390
W-Wait a minute!

00:12:49.500 --> 00:12:50.890
Should we be telling such a lie?

00:12:51.330 --> 00:12:53.330
Think of the people from
Mars who wanna go home...!

00:12:53.330 --> 00:12:54.530
Shut up, Kouji!

00:12:54.530 --> 00:12:55.070
But...!

00:12:55.070 --> 00:12:58.040
I take it that you're disagreeing
because you have an alternative plan.

00:12:58.440 --> 00:12:59.060
Well...!

00:12:59.840 --> 00:13:02.830
Your opinion is just, and I
can understand how you feel.

00:13:03.610 --> 00:13:06.680
However, there's no way we can
protect everyone that way, is there?

00:13:06.680 --> 00:13:08.680
Stop taking the matter lightly
at such a time as this!

00:13:08.680 --> 00:13:11.750
But people will eventually find
out the truth. If that happens...!

00:13:11.750 --> 00:13:13.410
We haven't got time!

00:13:13.950 --> 00:13:16.160
This isn't the time to be
acting like "Mr. Nice Guy"!

00:13:16.160 --> 00:13:18.520
It's impossible to convince everyone,
and taking the situation lightly...

00:13:18.520 --> 00:13:21.590
...by spending precious time thinking,
is only gonna get all of us killed!

00:13:21.590 --> 00:13:22.830
All of us!

00:13:22.830 --> 00:13:27.300
Controlling information allows us to lead
the public without causing confusion.

00:13:27.300 --> 00:13:29.360
We would be wise to take
whatever steps are best for us.

00:13:29.800 --> 00:13:31.170
Something a realist would say.

00:13:31.940 --> 00:13:35.440
Are you trying to continue this
discussion on a meaningless level?

00:13:35.440 --> 00:13:36.410
No.

00:13:38.580 --> 00:13:39.670
Okay, it's decided.

00:13:40.180 --> 00:13:42.010
I'll go through the ship
and persuade everyone.

00:13:42.550 --> 00:13:45.610
They're more likely to listen to us
than Zwei or supervisors. Rally! Marco!

00:13:45.790 --> 00:13:46.950
As you wish.

00:13:46.950 --> 00:13:47.610
All right.

00:13:47.820 --> 00:13:51.850
Also, Faina, I want you to
make the initial announcement.

00:13:53.430 --> 00:13:55.790
If Kouji said it, people
would see through the lie.

00:13:56.430 --> 00:13:57.400
O-Okay.

00:14:06.010 --> 00:14:07.270
It's the next one.

00:14:07.270 --> 00:14:11.770
The Bratica created a gravitational
field during Mission Plan YS-45.

00:14:25.930 --> 00:14:31.450
Radius of 7.4 serade, space curve
rate of the gravitational field, 6. 1

00:14:31.900 --> 00:14:34.390
It's a low figure for a Vaia ship...!

00:14:34.730 --> 00:14:37.130
And it's aimless, it spreads spherically.

00:14:37.370 --> 00:14:40.170
We can only assume the control
system was purposely turned off.

00:14:40.440 --> 00:14:41.910
Look at this next document.

00:14:43.810 --> 00:14:46.510
It's defended itself against
a Bosscon type torpedo...

00:14:47.050 --> 00:14:49.640
...shot from submersible ship
Tandel, by creating a field.

00:14:52.450 --> 00:14:55.790
The crew appears to be well trained.

00:14:56.160 --> 00:14:59.020
But why didn't they attack
the submersible ship?

00:14:59.430 --> 00:15:01.760
Perhaps to demonstrate
their defense-only policy.

00:15:03.130 --> 00:15:06.190
The number one public enemy
has a defense-only policy?

00:15:06.700 --> 00:15:10.290
However, once in the Mars vicinity,
the Bratica changes tactics and attacks.

00:15:11.000 --> 00:15:13.100
In its battle against the
Mars Space Navigation Forces...

00:15:13.340 --> 00:15:16.470
...it fired its main cannon located
on the ship's portside, just once.

00:15:18.380 --> 00:15:19.550
The Barge Cannon.

00:15:19.550 --> 00:15:21.380
Adaptation of a Linear Railgun.

00:15:22.180 --> 00:15:24.550
Taking into consideration the time
it took for them to reach the fleet...

00:15:24.920 --> 00:15:27.550
...we can also assume they're
using a gravitational system.

00:15:28.420 --> 00:15:32.150
The proof is that it wasn't used after
its separation with the Lift Ship.

00:15:49.180 --> 00:15:50.570
Vital Guarder?

00:15:50.940 --> 00:15:51.880
Einvalt.

00:15:52.680 --> 00:15:54.650
The Vital Guarder operates
by remote control...

00:15:54.650 --> 00:15:57.280
...from the transport carrier Lift
Ship that serves as the booster.

00:15:58.050 --> 00:16:01.750
The puppet wire used for operating
is made of TN material, type 2.

00:16:02.790 --> 00:16:06.420
If used together with gravitational control,
it can even be used past Sere 1.

00:16:07.160 --> 00:16:11.760
The gravitational field released during
the Vital Guarder's battle against...

00:16:12.170 --> 00:16:15.160
...the Mars Space Navigation Forces had
a maximum space curve rate of 36.

00:16:15.770 --> 00:16:17.170
36?

00:16:17.700 --> 00:16:22.370
That's high enough to render an attack
from any existing weapon ineffective.

00:16:22.540 --> 00:16:26.000
It would be safe to assume that
the system is fully operational.

00:16:26.850 --> 00:16:28.480
The system is one thing...

00:16:28.480 --> 00:16:30.850
...but what's particularly puzzling
are the actions taken by the Bratica.

00:16:31.380 --> 00:16:33.940
Although part of it may have
to do with our attack in waves...

00:16:34.490 --> 00:16:36.750
...I can't find an objective in their actions.

00:16:39.330 --> 00:16:43.630
Your job is to predict the Bratica's actions,
based on what they've done to this point.

00:16:44.630 --> 00:16:47.400
Vice-Minister Berkovich is
counting on you men a great deal.

00:16:47.400 --> 00:16:48.870
Be well aware of that.

00:16:49.870 --> 00:16:52.630
No matter who's on this ship,
and for what purpose...

00:16:53.170 --> 00:16:55.440
...we must get our hands on it.

00:16:56.180 --> 00:17:00.370
It's all... Yes, it's all to
find a future for humankind.

00:17:10.560 --> 00:17:11.890
Come on. Hurry up.

00:17:12.530 --> 00:17:13.560
It won't fit.

00:17:13.560 --> 00:17:14.960
You've got pockets, right?

00:17:14.960 --> 00:17:17.450
At times like these, the people
with food are the biggest winners.

00:17:19.900 --> 00:17:24.600
In the end... In the end, Charlotte
and I will experience the same fate.

00:17:25.140 --> 00:17:27.110
This is an ordeal granted to me by God.

00:17:27.410 --> 00:17:30.270
So that our destined relationship
will be a strong one.

00:17:30.510 --> 00:17:33.340
Must be nice to have your desire
take priority over everything else.

00:17:34.850 --> 00:17:36.780
Charlotte!

00:17:37.420 --> 00:17:40.850
What'll we do? What do you think
we should do from now on, Nicks?

00:17:41.090 --> 00:17:44.060
Things will work themselves out.
We're innocent, after all.

00:17:44.560 --> 00:17:47.030
That's true, but... Hey,
what should we do, Nicks?

00:17:47.390 --> 00:17:50.090
Would you be quiet?
There's nothing we can do!

00:17:52.700 --> 00:17:53.260
Hi!

00:17:54.730 --> 00:17:56.170
How'd the meeting go?

00:17:56.170 --> 00:17:58.140
Listen to the announcement.

00:17:58.700 --> 00:18:00.330
So we <i>are</i> leaving Mars.

00:18:01.610 --> 00:18:04.870
Which means the Vital Guarder is
on standby, prepared to battle.

00:18:05.380 --> 00:18:07.140
Want help with the controls?

00:18:07.280 --> 00:18:08.310
You sure you know how?

00:18:08.310 --> 00:18:10.620
You mustn't judge people by their looks.

00:18:10.620 --> 00:18:12.350
That's usually a comment used when
talking of others, not oneself.

00:18:12.350 --> 00:18:15.810
Judge me with the results.
And be prepared to be surprised.

00:18:16.490 --> 00:18:18.150
Do as you wish.

00:18:20.390 --> 00:18:22.380
Reiko. You mustn't cry.

00:18:22.860 --> 00:18:26.350
Did we do anything wrong?
No, we haven't done anything wrong!

00:18:26.570 --> 00:18:27.500
But, still...!

00:18:27.630 --> 00:18:30.000
You've gotta do something about the
way you get so easily depressed!

00:18:30.440 --> 00:18:32.370
Kozue, could you talk to her?

00:18:37.340 --> 00:18:38.440
Ikumi...!

00:18:39.350 --> 00:18:40.570
Hi.

00:18:41.280 --> 00:18:42.470
Ikumi!

00:18:44.020 --> 00:18:44.980
Don't worry.

00:18:45.690 --> 00:18:49.310
I'll protect you. No matter
what happens, I'll protect you.

00:18:49.660 --> 00:18:51.620
How can you say so in
the situation we're in?

00:18:51.760 --> 00:18:53.250
Yeah, really.

00:18:54.160 --> 00:18:55.960
<i>This is an announcement from the bridge.</i>

00:18:55.960 --> 00:18:58.200
<i>We have encountered an</i>
<i>emergency situation.</i>

00:18:58.200 --> 00:19:01.300
<i>A fleet of the Mars Forces, greater than</i>
<i>any we've encountered to this point...</i>

00:19:01.300 --> 00:19:03.000
<i>... is coming in the Ryvius's direction.</i>

00:19:03.000 --> 00:19:06.410
<i>We received a message, regarding their</i>
<i>attack plans, and battle is unavoidable.</i>

00:19:06.410 --> 00:19:08.270
<i>For the safety of all aboard,</i>
<i>we have decided to leave Mars.</i>

00:19:09.180 --> 00:19:14.670
<i>We must act quickly. We ask for</i>
<i>your understanding of the situation.</i>

00:19:15.380 --> 00:19:17.980
<i>I repeat. We have encountered an!</i>

00:19:17.980 --> 00:19:18.850
You're kidding!

00:19:18.850 --> 00:19:21.190
No! We can't leave Mars!

00:19:21.190 --> 00:19:24.560
<i>We received a message, regarding</i>
<i>their attack plans, and battle...!</i>

00:19:24.560 --> 00:19:27.290
<i>Ikumi. Are you really sure</i>
<i>this is the best option?</i>

00:19:27.990 --> 00:19:31.620
<i>If you do too much for your own sake,</i>
<i>you'll pay for it later. Without a doubt.</i>

00:19:35.330 --> 00:19:41.400
<i>We have escaped from the accident on</i>
<i>Astronaut Training Center, Liebe Delta.</i>

00:19:41.870 --> 00:19:44.600
<i>We are currently aboard a
<i>spaceship called the Ryvius.</i></i>

00:19:44.910 --> 00:19:48.310
<i>487 people are stranded here.</i>
<i>Please hurry and rescue!</i>

00:19:49.250 --> 00:19:52.620
It's from the records we got from
the black box retrieved from Abend 2.

00:19:53.290 --> 00:19:56.590
I wanted your opinion, since you were
directly involved in battle with the Bratica.

00:19:57.120 --> 00:19:58.590
My opinion, sir?

00:20:01.130 --> 00:20:04.860
C-Captain... the people aboard
the Bratica... they're all...!

00:20:05.330 --> 00:20:10.290
My guess is that this transmission
is a bluff. In other words, it's a lie.

00:20:10.840 --> 00:20:12.340
Take the gravitational control of the Bratica...

00:20:12.340 --> 00:20:14.700
...the firing of the main cannon, and
the activation of the Vital Guarder.

00:20:15.010 --> 00:20:18.970
None of these things are possible,
unless someone on board knows the Vaia.

00:20:19.350 --> 00:20:23.580
I'm sure the terrorists on the Bratica forced
a student hostage to send this message...

00:20:23.580 --> 00:20:25.740
...to set us off guard.

00:20:26.550 --> 00:20:30.250
A strategic officer from Nierbara
had the exact same opinion.

00:20:30.490 --> 00:20:31.460
I'm honored.

00:20:31.720 --> 00:20:34.190
I just received a message
from Admiral Marley.

00:20:34.890 --> 00:20:38.890
He says that in addition to Impulse and
Dicastia, they're also recalling Gespenst.

00:20:39.470 --> 00:20:42.230
Gespenst? Back to the solar system?

00:20:42.770 --> 00:20:44.840
The people higher up have no
knowledge of the battlefield.

00:20:44.840 --> 00:20:47.000
They have no idea what this will do.

00:20:51.710 --> 00:20:55.200
Ryvius has successfully altered
course onto a swing-by-route.

00:20:55.850 --> 00:20:59.550
<i>We will begin our acceleration</i>
<i>in 38 minutes to leave Mars.</i>

00:21:00.050 --> 00:21:03.820
<i>You may feel tremors during this acceleration.</i>
<i>Please act with extra caution.</i>

00:21:04.890 --> 00:21:06.860
Why? Why?!

00:21:07.230 --> 00:21:08.190
Kouji.

00:21:14.900 --> 00:21:15.870
Faina.

00:21:16.800 --> 00:21:17.640
Kouji.

00:21:17.640 --> 00:21:23.230
I don't understand. How can
you be so calm? I'm... scared.

00:21:23.980 --> 00:21:25.880
It's like there's no ground, and...

00:21:25.880 --> 00:21:27.440
...we're just drifting in outer space.

00:21:28.480 --> 00:21:32.010
Why is this? I'm so scared!

00:21:32.990 --> 00:21:35.150
Kouji. That's great.

00:21:38.390 --> 00:21:40.360
The mercy of Holy Mother Arne.

00:21:40.790 --> 00:21:43.920
You have taken a step toward
freedom, as you wished.

00:21:45.630 --> 00:21:50.260
For you were able to sever the ties you
had with the society you hate so much.

00:21:51.370 --> 00:21:53.670
I believe that is a wonderful thing.

00:22:01.150 --> 00:22:03.740
One month has passed since that day.

00:22:08.110 --> 00:22:12.380
In your dry eyes...

00:22:12.380 --> 00:22:17.450
...a silhouette appears

00:22:17.450 --> 00:22:22.160
The blue colored future...

00:22:22.160 --> 00:22:28.890
...swayed and glittered

00:22:30.060 --> 00:22:38.300
Ah... No one wants...

00:22:38.300 --> 00:22:46.910
...freedom out of pity

00:22:46.910 --> 00:22:55.350
Ah... To the days I feared...

00:22:55.350 --> 00:22:59.260
...that I'd end up hurting someone,

00:22:59.260 --> 00:23:05.630
goodbye

00:23:09.650 --> 00:23:11.090
Infinite Ryvius

00:23:11.090 --> 00:23:12.890
Infinite Ryvius
Next episode: If Only to Meet
Because we'd been
closed off from our future...

00:23:12.890 --> 00:23:14.230
Next episode: If Only to Meet
...the top priority in our daily lives...

00:23:14.230 --> 00:23:15.790
Next episode: If Only to Meet
...was just to survive.

00:23:15.790 --> 00:23:16.830
Next episode: If Only to Meet

00:23:16.830 --> 00:23:18.900
Next episode: If Only to Meet
Anxiety bears heavily down on us.

00:23:18.900 --> 00:23:21.400
Next episode: If Only to Meet
I wanna escape.
I wanna run away from here.

00:23:21.400 --> 00:23:24.070
Next episode: If Only to Meet
Such feelings bring
people closer together.

00:23:24.070 --> 00:23:25.040
Next episode: If Only to Meet

00:23:25.040 --> 00:23:26.400
Next episode: If Only to Meet
What more can we do now...

00:23:26.400 --> 00:23:27.910
Next episode: If Only to Meet
...than to touch one another...

00:23:27.910 --> 00:23:28.210
Next episode: If Only to Meet

00:23:28.210 --> 00:23:29.930
Next episode: If Only to Meet
...to forget about now...
